# Retired routes (ADR-0012). The pages are gone but the URLs are still in
# Google's index and in old links, so they get a permanent redirect rather than
# a 404 — a bare 404 throws away whatever signal those URLs accumulated.
# Same six rules as `redirects()` in next.config.ts; verified against the live
# site in the Phase 4 checklist.
/leaderboard / 301
/monitor / 301
/evidence / 301
/timeline / 301
/videos / 301
/profile/:nickname / 301

# The demos column was deleted on 2026-09-23: it was a mis-translation of the reference
# site's /x-posts hub, and the seven rows in it were posts that already live in
# /typesafe-jev/x-posts (lib/jev-x-posts.ts has the full account). It never shipped to
# production — this only catches preview links and screenshots taken while it existed.
/typesafe-jev/demos /typesafe-jev/x-posts 308

# The Jev explainer pages moved under the topic prefix on 2026-09-23, hours after they
# shipped at the root. The rule they were moved to live by: **the root belongs to the site's
# own subject** (the OpenRouter catalogue and the Alpha line — the domain is literally named
# after it), and **every other model topic gets a prefix of its own**, because more are
# coming. A Jev page at `/jev-pricing` reads as if Jev were the site.
#
# 301 rather than 308: these are permanent moves of content whose search intent has not
# changed, and the old URLs were submitted to IndexNow the hour they went live, so the
# redirect is load-bearing rather than decorative.
/jev-pricing /typesafe-jev/pricing 301
/jev-vs-llm /typesafe-jev/vs-llm 301
/open-source-jev /typesafe-jev/open-source 301
/jev-guide /typesafe-jev/guide 301
